# Create Pull Request Workflow

- Delegate the PR title and body to the `PrAuthor` sub-agent (read-only: branch diff + linked GitHub issues).
- Write the drafted body to a temp file. Do not run `yarn ai:create-pr` without `--title` and `--body-file`.
- If `PrAuthor` fails (`ON_BASE_BRANCH:` / `NO_BRANCH_COMMITS:`), stop and report; do not create a subject-only PR.
- Run `corepack yarn ai:create-pr --title "<title>" --body-file <path>`.
- If reviewers are explicitly provided, pass `--reviewer <login>` for each one. Pass `--draft` when asked.
- Push upstream if needed, assign the authenticated GitHub user, and leave reviewers empty otherwise.
- Return the PR URL and the title on success.
